============================================================
                     HYPEROPERATOR LADDER
============================================================

Notation:
    a ↑^k b  = k-arrow hyperoperator on a, b
    For small k, we use standard up-arrow shorthands:

    k = 1 : a ↑ b      = a^b
    k = 2 : a ↑↑ b     = tetration
    k = 3 : a ↑↑↑ b    = pentation
    k = 4 : a ↑↑↑↑ b   = hexation
    ...

------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 1: EXPONENTIATION (↑)
------------------------------------------------------------

    a ↑ b = a^b

Examples:
    3 ↑ 2 = 3^2 = 9
    3 ↑ 3 = 3^3 = 27

------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 2: TETRATION (↑↑)
------------------------------------------------------------

    a ↑↑ b = a^(a^(...^a))   (b times, right-associated)

Examples:
    3 ↑↑ 2 = 3^3 = 27
    3 ↑↑ 3 = 3^(3^3) = 3^27

------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 3: PENTATION (↑↑↑)
------------------------------------------------------------

    a ↑↑↑ b = hyper-tetration of height b

Informally:
    a ↑↑↑ b = a ↑↑ (a ↑↑ (... ↑↑ a))   (b times)

Example (symbolic only):
    3 ↑↑↑ 2 = 3 ↑↑ (3 ↑↑ 3)

------------------------------------------------------------
LEVEL 4: HEXATION (↑↑↑↑)
------------------------------------------------------------

    a ↑↑↑↑ b = hyper-pentation of height b

Example (symbolic only):
    3 ↑↑↑↑ 3 = 3 ↑↑↑ (3 ↑↑↑ (3 ↑↑↑ 3))

------------------------------------------------------------
GENERAL LEVEL k: a ↑^k b
------------------------------------------------------------

    a ↑^1 b = a^b
    a ↑^2 b = a ↑↑ b
    a ↑^3 b = a ↑↑↑ b
    a ↑^4 b = a ↑↑↑↑ b
    ...
    a ↑^k b = "k-th hyperoperation" on a, b

