              ALGEBRA FOR THE GRAHAM SEQUENCE
============================================================
1. INDEX SET (GRADING)
============================================================

    K = { 4, g(1), g(2), ..., g(63) }

Interpretation:
    - Each k ∈ K is an operator index.
    - This plays the role of the graded dimensions.
    - Enormous, sparse grading (like huge graded pieces).

Grading rule:
    deg(H(k)) = k

2. OPERATOR FAMILY (ALGEBRA GENERATORS)
============================================================

Define:
    H(k) = "k-arrow hyperoperator on base 3"

Action:
    H(k)(3,3) = 3 ↑^k 3

Operator algebra:
    A = { H(k) : k ∈ K }

Composition:

    H(k1) ∘ H(k2) = H( k1 ⋆ k2 )

where ⋆ is the induced operator-index composition.

3. STATE SPACE (REPRESENTATION SPACE)
============================================================

    G = { g(1), g(2), ..., g(64) }

Generation rule:
    g(1)   = H(4)(3,3)
    g(n+1) = H(g(n))(3,3)

Interpretation:
    - G is a distinguished orbit under A.
    - Analogous to a special Monster representation.

4. ACTION (REPRESENTATION)
============================================================

Define action of A on the base state 3:

    H(k) ⋅ 3 = H(k)(3,3)

Recursive representation:
    g(1)   = H(4) ⋅ 3
    g(2)   = H(g(1)) ⋅ 3
    g(3)   = H(g(2)) ⋅ 3
    ...
